  "summary": "Thai art refers to a diverse range of art forms created in Thailand from prehistoric times to the present day, including architecture, sculpture, painting, textiles, decorative arts, crafts, ceramics, and more.",
  "description": "Thai art refers to a diverse range of art forms created in Thailand from prehistoric times to the present day, including architecture, sculpture, painting, textiles, decorative arts, crafts, ceramics, and more. Buddhism has shaped much of Thai art, and many sculptures and paintings depict Buddha images and religious themes. But nature, including flora and fauna, as well as mythical creatures, has been a major inspiration for Thai art, with colorful motifs appearing in different types of art forms. In contemporary Thai art, traditional works remain significant and continue to influence artists' concepts.",
